Provide a restartable stop operation that joins the statistics finalizer
before the store is closed. Serialize stop, resume and disposal so a
second closer cannot return while the first is still using SQLite. Route
acceptance to the reply server when the receive queue is already
secured, and keep the local LET command independent of receive-server
ACK retries.

Recheck pending deliveries after retry delays and join replaced queue
workers. Avoid retrying cached messages deleted while the server was
offline.

Stop XFTP workers before their transports; recheck cached deliveries
after both retry delays and suspension/network waits.

Serialize async ACK registration with receive/delete processing; do not
queue a second ACK for an already acknowledged stored message. Preserve
interactive request mode when creating a contact-link reply queue.

